    "unit": "J/mol",
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "hint": "Use $\\Delta \\kAmolar = \\kR\\kT(y_1\\ln y_1 + y_2\\ln y_2)$ from Example 22.1.1.",
    "solution": "<p>With $y_1 = y_2 = 0.5$ the sum is $0.5\\ln 0.5 + 0.5\\ln 0.5 = \\ln 0.5 = -0.6931$. Then $\\Delta \\kAmolar = (8.314\\ \\text{J K}^{-1}\\text{mol}^{-1})(298.15\\ \\text{K})(-0.6931) = -1718$ J/mol. It is negative, as it must be for a spontaneous change at constant $\\kT$ and $\\kV$, and since $\\kDeltaU = 0$ all of it is $-\\kT\\Delta \\kSent$.</p>"
